 "seesTitle": "What Es Caragol sees",
 "seesHTML": "A wild, roadless beach behind the island's southern tip: 20 minutes on foot from the Cap de ses Salines lighthouse road, and the reward is a pure sea horizon \u2014 totality with \u22482.2\u00b0 to spare and the eclipsed crescent dissolving into the Mediterranean. No facilities, no light, no shade; the walk back is by headlamp.",
 "capHTML": "Horizon panorama from Es Caragol: terrain silhouettes with projected angular altitudes against the sun's descent. The crescent is last visible at \u224820:46.",
 "recoTitle": "Around Es Caragol",
 "recoHTML": "<li><b>The west-facing strand</b> \u2014 walk past the dune point until the WNW water is open.</li><li><b>Cap de ses Salines lighthouse</b> \u2014 drive-up alternative at the trailhead; a low inland rise takes the last partial minutes there (see its row).</li>",
 "verdictText": "Full show \u2014 totality, then the crescent sets into the sea at \u224820:46"
